1
00:05:13,333 --> 00:05:19,333
Dying of the Light is a thriller, drama film directed by Paul Schrader.

2
00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:32,666
Evan Lake, a veteran CIA agent, has been ordered to retire.

3
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:46,000
But when his protégé uncovers evidence that Lake's nemesis, the terrorist Banir, has resurfaced, Lake
goes rogue, embarking on a perilous, intercontinental mission to eliminate his sworn enemy.

4
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:59,333
Evan Lake, played by Nicolas Cage.

5
00:26:06,666 --> 00:26:12,666
Milton Schultz, played by Anton Yelchin.

6
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Muhammad Banir, played by Alexander Karim.

7
00:36:33,333 --> 00:36:39,333
Michelle Zuberain, played by Irène Jacob.

8
00:41:46,666 --> 00:41:52,666
Aasim, played by Aymen Hamdouchi.

9
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Mbui, played by Tomiwa Edun.

10
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:19,333
Dying of the Light is a 2014 American spy film,
written and directed by Paul Schrader.

11
00:57:26,666 --> 00:57:32,666
It stars Nicolas Cage as an ex-CIA agent suffering from dementia who is on a personal mission
to track down and kill a terrorist who had tortured him two decades earlier.

12
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Anton Yelchin and Irène Jacob also feature in the cast.

13
01:07:53,333 --> 01:07:59,333
Dying of the Light was released theatrically and through VOD formats by Lionsgate on
December 5, 2014 to extremely negative reviews from film critics.

14
01:13:06,666 --> 01:13:12,666
Schrader was denied final-cut privilege by the studio, who
heavily reedited the footage without his consent.

15
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
Schrader and his principal cast subsequently disowned the
released version of the film and campaigned against it.

16
01:23:33,333 --> 01:23:39,333
The film explores themes of central intelligence agency
(cia), espionage, retirement, terrorism.

17
01:28:46,666 --> 01:28:52,666
The tone is emotional and intense.
